{
  "format": "bgsim.model",
  "language": "0.1.0",
  "name": "two-mass",
  "$comment": "Plan 9.6b industrial-servo (X2.6). The PMSM plant is a bond graph (D28): d/q 1-junctions with R and I, an MGY cross-coupling w_e L from a Gain of the measured speed, an MSe back-EMF k_e w_m (the junction sees -k_e w_m), and a GY k_t = 1.5 p psi_m to the mechanical 1-junction (the measured i_q drives the GY through an MSf, which closes the dq 3/2 power convention). The rotor is I(J_m)+R(B_m); the load is either rigid or an I-C-R two-mass coupling. Sensors: FlowSensors, the kinematic Theta integrator and, in the encoder variants, a 24-bit Quantizer and the SpeedEstimator. The only code is the sampled firmware (ServoCurrentLoop 8 kHz, ServoSpeedLoop 1 kHz, ServoPositionLoop 200 Hz) and the switching inverter (PwmInverter). Variant: flexible I-C-R two-mass coupling + notch; averaged inverter; ideal encoder.",
